{"name":"Matriarch","hex":"#7e6884","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"matriarch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female leader of a family, a tribe or an ethnic or religious group.\n\nThe dominant female in a family group of elephants.\n A strong and domineering older woman; a battle axe.","The dominant female in a family group of elephants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matriarch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Matriarch (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Matriarch is the fifth studio album by American metalcore band Veil of Maya. It is the band's first album with vocalist Lukas Magyar. The album was produced, mixed and mastered by Taylor Larson of From First to Last."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Matriarch_%28Veil_of_Maya%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matriarch_(album)","wikidata":"Q19954594"},{"title":"Matriarch (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Matriarch is a 2022 American horror film written and directed by Ben Steiner and starring Jemima Rooper and Kate Dickie."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/Matriarch_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matriarch_(film)","wikidata":"Q115474904"},{"title":"Matriarchy","blocks":[{"text":"Matriarchy is a social system in which positions of power and privilege are primarily held by women. In a broader sense it can also extend to moral authority, social privilege, and control of property. While those definitions apply in general English, definitions specific to anthropology and feminism differ in some respect."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matriarchy","wikidata":"Q185681"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Coyolxauhqui_4095977415_b89d64f008-2.jpg/500px-Coyolxauhqui_4095977415_b89d64f008-2.jpg?utm_sourc